  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wefaq society for women and child care</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Act 1.1.1 Coordinate distribution of Adolescent Girl Humanitarian Package to adolescent girls in different locations and IDP shelters.
Wefaq will work with UNRWA and Government shelters in Rafah with people who recently evacuated from the North, in addition to IDP families in hosted communities in Rafah, reaching in total 1230 individuals in coordination with other partners

Act 1.1.2 Awareness raising and recreational activities for adolescent girls tailored to their specific protection concerns and their wellbeing
Wefaqwill provide recreational activities, establish self-help group, provide awareness sessions on health and protection in UNRWA, informal and governmental shelters in Rafah.

Act 1.1.3 Support partnered women&#x2019;s led organisations continued programming via small scale funds for operations in case of need
 activity will entail provision of the financial support to Wefaq of between 8,000 and 10,000EUR (depending on partner capacity) to allow for a flexible allocation of the small-scale financial support to cover the most urgent organizational / operational needs.

Act 1.2.1 Coordinate distribution of supplements and other nutrition supplements to pregnant and lactating women and adolescent girls in different locations and IDP shelters
Wefaq will work with UNRWA and Government shelters in Rafah with people who recently evacuated from the North, and hosted community in Rafah, selecting estimated 995 women and girls.

Act 1.3.1 Conduct assessments in &#x2018;hot spot&#x2019; locations (hospitals, shelters, etc.) to identify, register (using UNICEF Platform) andrefer cases of Unaccompanied and Separated Children
Oxfam and child protection partners (Wefaq, Atfaluna, AISHA) will define and update ways of working in close coordination with UNICEF and the CP AoR, based on criteria and referral pathways shared.</narrative>
  </description>
