  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wefaq Association for Women and Child Care is an independent, non-profit Palestinian women&#x2019;s association established in 2010, aiming to achieve gender equality through economic empowerment and psychological support programs to support marginalized groupsin the southern Gaza Strip, especially in the governorates of Rafah and Khan Yunis. From 1996 until 2009 under the name of the Women&#x2019;s Department, where it was working under the umbrella of the Gaza Mental Health Program, and due to the change in policiesand the expansion of the program&#x2019;s field of work into a knowledge-based organization focusing on practical research, training and advocacy, a restructuring process for the program took place which This resulted in the development of the Women&apos;s Departmentinto an independent association under the name Wefaq Association for the Care of Women and Children with license number (8155).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wefaq Society for Women and Child C</narrative>
  </participating-org>
